From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:16:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clutter/color: Decide mapping once per source and target pair

Direct scanout asks clutter_color_transform_requires_mapping() for
every frame and the hardware cursor plane for every pointer motion, and
the gamut part computed Bradford adaptations and matrix inversions
before it could find the content within the target, every time.

Make the decision once per pair of color states and keep it with the
transform cache, under the same exact key (without flags, which do not
take part), invalidated when either state is destroyed, like the
transforms. The highlight and gamut predicates, the combined predicate
and the transform builder all read the one recorded decision, gamut
compression limits included, so scanout, the cursor plane and the
renderer still cannot diverge; there is no second decision path.

A new test checks that the pipeline holds the mapping ops exactly when
the predicates say so, on repeated questions, and that a decision ends
with its states.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
